1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,065
Your build works. The jar sits on your laptop. And your teammate cannot use it.

2
00:00:05,615 --> 00:00:06,940
Until you publish it,

3
00:00:06,940 --> 00:00:09,715
to the repository your whole company shares.

4
00:00:09,715 --> 00:00:11,418
That step is called deploy.

5
00:00:11,968 --> 00:00:14,348
Today you learn the two kinds of version,

6
00:00:14,348 --> 00:00:15,567
snapshot and release,

7
00:00:15,567 --> 00:00:18,005
and the one rule that surprises everybody.

8
00:00:18,555 --> 00:00:21,094
Then you publish, and break the rule on purpose.

9
00:00:21,644 --> 00:00:22,865
This is CloudCart,

10
00:00:22,865 --> 00:00:25,646
the app we build all through this course.

11
00:00:25,646 --> 00:00:27,817
Version zero is a Maven project.

12
00:00:27,817 --> 00:00:32,769
Today its cart core module becomes a package your teammates can download.

13
00:00:32,769 --> 00:00:33,176
Later,

14
00:00:33,176 --> 00:00:34,872
in the nexus masterclass,

15
00:00:34,872 --> 00:00:36,907
you repeat this on real nexus,

16
00:00:36,907 --> 00:00:40,503
and CloudCart version one wires it into the pipeline.

17
00:00:41,053 --> 00:00:42,180
One honest note.

18
00:00:42,180 --> 00:00:44,856
The repository in this lesson is real.

19
00:00:44,856 --> 00:00:47,111
It is Sonatype Nexus Repository,

20
00:00:47,111 --> 00:00:48,378
Community Edition,

21
00:00:48,378 --> 00:00:49,928
running on my machine.

22
00:00:49,928 --> 00:00:52,816
Its license agreement is yours to accept,

23
00:00:52,816 --> 00:00:55,986
and it needs about three gigabytes of memory.

24
00:00:57,536 --> 00:01:01,316
Install copies your jar into your own dot m two folder.

25
00:01:01,316 --> 00:01:04,133
Deploy uploads it to a remote repository,

26
00:01:04,133 --> 00:01:05,920
so others can download it.

27
00:01:06,470 --> 00:01:09,948
A repository manager usually has two repositories,

28
00:01:09,948 --> 00:01:12,660
one for snapshots and one for releases.

29
00:01:12,660 --> 00:01:15,164
You create each one in its web page,

30
00:01:15,164 --> 00:01:18,225
and choose its type and its redeploy policy.

31
00:01:18,775 --> 00:01:20,642
A snapshot is work in progress.

32
00:01:20,642 --> 00:01:22,810
The version ends with dash snapshot.

33
00:01:22,810 --> 00:01:24,919
You may publish it again and again.

34
00:01:25,469 --> 00:01:30,909
A release is final. The version has no snapshot. Once published, it can never be replaced.

35
00:01:31,459 --> 00:01:33,304
The pom says where to upload.

36
00:01:33,304 --> 00:01:35,658
In the block distribution management,

37
00:01:35,658 --> 00:01:37,312
one address for snapshots,

38
00:01:37,312 --> 00:01:38,648
and one for releases.

39
00:01:40,698 --> 00:01:44,517
Why can a release never be replaced? Because other people built on it.

40
00:01:45,067 --> 00:01:48,453
If the jar for one dot zero dot zero changed tomorrow,

41
00:01:48,453 --> 00:01:50,648
an old build could not be repeated.

42
00:01:50,648 --> 00:01:53,344
The same version would mean different code.

43
00:01:53,894 --> 00:01:55,755
So the repository refuses.

44
00:01:55,755 --> 00:01:57,472
It answers four oh nine,

45
00:01:57,472 --> 00:01:58,117
conflict.

46
00:01:58,117 --> 00:02:00,693
The right fix is never to overwrite.

47
00:02:00,693 --> 00:02:02,769
Publish one dot zero dot one.

48
00:02:03,319 --> 00:02:04,951
A snapshot is different.

49
00:02:04,951 --> 00:02:06,583
Maven adds a time stamp,

50
00:02:06,583 --> 00:02:08,556
so each upload is a new file,

51
00:02:08,556 --> 00:02:10,188
and the newest one wins.

52
00:02:10,738 --> 00:02:11,634
And the login?

53
00:02:11,634 --> 00:02:13,170
The same as last lesson.

54
00:02:13,170 --> 00:02:14,130
A server block,

55
00:02:14,130 --> 00:02:15,218
with the same id,

56
00:02:15,218 --> 00:02:18,162
and the password from an environment variable.

57
00:02:20,212 --> 00:02:21,688
Start in the browser.

58
00:02:21,688 --> 00:02:22,883
Go to local host,

59
00:02:22,883 --> 00:02:24,500
port eighty-eighty-one.

60
00:02:24,500 --> 00:02:27,523
This is the real Sonatype Nexus Repository,

61
00:02:27,523 --> 00:02:28,788
Community Edition.

62
00:02:31,338 --> 00:02:37,203
The login page tells you where the first password lives: a file called admin dot password.

63
00:02:37,203 --> 00:02:38,245
In your own lab,

64
00:02:38,245 --> 00:02:39,223
read that file,

65
00:02:39,223 --> 00:02:40,917
and paste the password in.

66
00:02:40,917 --> 00:02:42,090
The user is admin.

67
00:02:49,640 --> 00:02:52,432
Nexus now makes you choose your own password.

68
00:02:52,432 --> 00:02:53,549
Pick a strong one,

69
00:02:53,549 --> 00:02:55,224
and keep it somewhere safe.

70
00:02:55,224 --> 00:02:57,520
This one is a throwaway for the demo.

71
00:02:57,520 --> 00:02:59,816
Never show a real password on screen.

72
00:03:05,366 --> 00:03:08,459
It signs you out, so log in again, with the new password.

73
00:03:16,009 --> 00:03:20,105
A short setup wizard starts. Step one is a welcome. Click next.

74
00:03:23,655 --> 00:03:25,908
Step two is the license agreement.

75
00:03:25,908 --> 00:03:26,969
In your own lab,

76
00:03:26,969 --> 00:03:27,499
read it,

77
00:03:27,499 --> 00:03:29,420
and accept only if you agree.

78
00:03:29,420 --> 00:03:30,348
For this demo,

79
00:03:30,348 --> 00:03:31,143
I accept it.

80
00:03:34,693 --> 00:03:36,696
Step three is anonymous access.

81
00:03:36,696 --> 00:03:37,859
Leave it disabled,

82
00:03:37,859 --> 00:03:41,477
so nobody can download your packages without logging in.

83
00:03:44,027 --> 00:03:46,165
Step four is a required notice.

84
00:03:46,165 --> 00:03:49,130
Nexus sends a small usage report every day.

85
00:03:49,130 --> 00:03:51,682
If it cannot be sent for thirty days,

86
00:03:51,682 --> 00:03:53,820
the instance becomes read only.

87
00:03:53,820 --> 00:03:54,716
Tick the box,

88
00:03:54,716 --> 00:03:55,889
and click finish.

89
00:04:01,439 --> 00:04:02,995
This is the dashboard.

90
00:04:02,995 --> 00:04:04,126
Now the sidebar,

91
00:04:04,126 --> 00:04:04,975
on the left.

92
00:04:04,975 --> 00:04:05,683
Dashboard.

93
00:04:05,683 --> 00:04:06,178
Search,

94
00:04:06,178 --> 00:04:07,451
to find a package.

95
00:04:07,451 --> 00:04:07,946
Browse,

96
00:04:07,946 --> 00:04:09,926
to look inside a repository.

97
00:04:09,926 --> 00:04:10,422
Upload,

98
00:04:10,422 --> 00:04:11,978
to add a file by hand.

99
00:04:11,978 --> 00:04:12,756
The shield,

100
00:04:12,756 --> 00:04:14,170
for security health.

101
00:04:14,170 --> 00:04:15,090
And the gear,

102
00:04:15,090 --> 00:04:16,009
for settings.

103
00:04:20,559 --> 00:04:23,262
Nexus has a new look and a classic look.

104
00:04:23,262 --> 00:04:25,491
Most guides show the classic one,

105
00:04:25,491 --> 00:04:27,585
so click switch to classic U I.

106
00:04:27,585 --> 00:04:28,531
Then the gear,

107
00:04:28,531 --> 00:04:29,409
for settings,

108
00:04:29,409 --> 00:04:30,558
and repositories.

109
00:04:30,558 --> 00:04:32,719
This list is the heart of Nexus.

110
00:04:34,269 --> 00:04:36,356
Each row is one repository.

111
00:04:36,356 --> 00:04:37,052
Its name.

112
00:04:37,052 --> 00:04:37,748
Its type,

113
00:04:37,748 --> 00:04:38,289
hosted,

114
00:04:38,289 --> 00:04:38,752
proxy,

115
00:04:38,752 --> 00:04:39,448
or group.

116
00:04:39,448 --> 00:04:40,298
Its format,

117
00:04:40,298 --> 00:04:41,458
here maven two.

118
00:04:41,458 --> 00:04:42,308
Its status.

119
00:04:42,308 --> 00:04:43,699
And a copy button,

120
00:04:43,699 --> 00:04:44,936
for its address.

121
00:04:45,486 --> 00:04:47,992
Hosted means it stores what you upload.

122
00:04:47,992 --> 00:04:50,692
Proxy means it fetches from another place,

123
00:04:50,692 --> 00:04:51,784
and keeps a copy.

124
00:04:51,784 --> 00:04:55,705
Group means it joins several repositories behind one address.

125
00:04:56,255 --> 00:04:57,758
Four came with Nexus.

126
00:04:57,758 --> 00:05:01,411
Maven central is a proxy of the real Maven Central.

127
00:05:01,411 --> 00:05:03,129
Maven public is a group.

128
00:05:03,129 --> 00:05:06,423
Maven releases and maven snapshots are hosted.

129
00:05:06,423 --> 00:05:08,142
Your team keeps its own.

130
00:05:08,142 --> 00:05:09,503
Let us create them.

131
00:05:11,053 --> 00:05:15,149
Click create repository. Choose the recipe, maven two, hosted.

132
00:05:27,699 --> 00:05:29,861
The name is corp dash snapshots.

133
00:05:29,861 --> 00:05:31,957
The version policy is snapshot,

134
00:05:31,957 --> 00:05:35,336
so this repository accepts only snapshot versions.

135
00:05:42,886 --> 00:05:45,499
The deployment policy is allow redeploy,

136
00:05:45,499 --> 00:05:48,373
because a snapshot is replaced all the time.

137
00:05:48,373 --> 00:05:49,157
Scroll down,

138
00:05:49,157 --> 00:05:50,267
and click create.

139
00:05:59,817 --> 00:06:03,849
Now the same again, for releases. The name is corp dash releases.

140
00:06:16,399 --> 00:06:18,445
The defaults are exactly right.

141
00:06:18,445 --> 00:06:20,424
The version policy is release.

142
00:06:20,424 --> 00:06:23,459
And the deployment policy is disable redeploy,

143
00:06:23,459 --> 00:06:26,428
so a published release can never be replaced.

144
00:06:26,428 --> 00:06:27,087
Create it.

145
00:06:35,637 --> 00:06:37,131
Two new repositories.

146
00:06:37,131 --> 00:06:38,908
Each has its own address,

147
00:06:38,908 --> 00:06:40,828
ending in slash repository,

148
00:06:40,828 --> 00:06:41,895
slash its name.

149
00:06:41,895 --> 00:06:44,171
Maven needs these two addresses.

150
00:06:46,721 --> 00:06:50,795
Now the terminal. Go to the demo project. Type: CD, demo.

151
00:06:51,345 --> 00:06:54,477
Look at the upload addresses in the pom.

152
00:06:54,477 --> 00:06:55,260
Type: sed,

153
00:06:55,260 --> 00:06:55,808
dash n,

154
00:06:55,808 --> 00:06:57,844
twelve comma twenty-one p,

155
00:06:57,844 --> 00:06:58,940
pom dot X M L.

156
00:06:59,490 --> 00:07:02,026
Snapshots go to corp dash snapshots.

157
00:07:02,026 --> 00:07:04,421
Releases go to corp dash releases.

158
00:07:04,421 --> 00:07:05,900
Both use the id corp,

159
00:07:05,900 --> 00:07:07,661
so one login serves both.

160
00:07:08,211 --> 00:07:09,397
Set the password from a locked file.

161
00:07:09,397 --> 00:07:11,142
Type: export N E X U S underscore PASS equals dollar,

162
00:07:11,142 --> 00:07:11,538
parenthesis,

163
00:07:11,538 --> 00:07:11,669
cat,

164
00:07:11,669 --> 00:07:11,867
tilde,

165
00:07:11,867 --> 00:07:12,065
slash,

166
00:07:12,065 --> 00:07:12,691
dot corp dash pass.

167
00:07:14,741 --> 00:07:15,390
Deploy the snapshot.

168
00:07:15,390 --> 00:07:15,780
Type: M V N,

169
00:07:15,780 --> 00:07:16,007
dash B,

170
00:07:16,007 --> 00:07:16,234
dash s,

171
00:07:16,234 --> 00:07:16,851
settings dot X M L,

172
00:07:16,851 --> 00:07:17,078
deploy.

173
00:07:17,078 --> 00:07:18,149
Then keep only the uploaded path,

174
00:07:18,149 --> 00:07:18,474
with grep.

175
00:07:19,424 --> 00:07:21,920
Maven builds, then uploads to Nexus.

176
00:07:34,470 --> 00:07:35,839
First the repository,

177
00:07:35,839 --> 00:07:37,142
corp dash snapshots.

178
00:07:37,142 --> 00:07:38,055
Then the path,

179
00:07:38,055 --> 00:07:40,075
and the jar name: a time stamp,

180
00:07:40,075 --> 00:07:41,313
and a build number,

181
00:07:41,313 --> 00:07:41,574
one.

182
00:07:42,124 --> 00:07:44,193
Deploy it again. The same command.

183
00:07:46,643 --> 00:07:47,838
A second upload.

184
00:07:57,388 --> 00:08:02,359
Build number two, a new time stamp. Nothing was replaced, and nothing was refused.

185
00:08:02,909 --> 00:08:08,562
Now make it a release. Remove the word snapshot from the version, with sed.

186
00:08:11,612 --> 00:08:14,940
Version one dot zero dot zero. No snapshot.

187
00:08:15,490 --> 00:08:16,642
Deploy it. The same command.

188
00:08:19,092 --> 00:08:20,287
Uploading the release.

189
00:08:29,837 --> 00:08:35,682
Published. This time the jar name has no time stamp. It is just one dot zero dot zero.

190
00:08:36,232 --> 00:08:41,437
Now the rule. Deploy the same version again, and keep only the line with the status code.

191
00:08:44,487 --> 00:08:46,301
Same version, second time.

192
00:08:55,851 --> 00:08:56,709
Four oh nine,

193
00:08:56,709 --> 00:08:57,303
conflict.

194
00:08:57,303 --> 00:08:59,877
Nexus says the redeploy is not allowed.

195
00:08:59,877 --> 00:09:01,527
The release is protected.

196
00:09:01,527 --> 00:09:02,781
To change anything,

197
00:09:02,781 --> 00:09:04,299
you need a new version.

198
00:09:04,849 --> 00:09:07,899
Back to the browser. Click browse, to see what arrived.

199
00:09:09,949 --> 00:09:15,048
Open corp dash snapshots. Nexus shows a tree. Group, project, then the version.

200
00:09:18,598 --> 00:09:21,271
Under one dot zero dot zero snapshot,

201
00:09:21,271 --> 00:09:22,138
two uploads.

202
00:09:22,138 --> 00:09:22,860
Build one,

203
00:09:22,860 --> 00:09:23,871
and build two.

204
00:09:23,871 --> 00:09:25,894
Each has its own time stamp.

205
00:09:28,444 --> 00:09:29,314
Click the jar.

206
00:09:29,314 --> 00:09:31,364
The summary names the repository,

207
00:09:31,364 --> 00:09:32,047
the format,

208
00:09:32,047 --> 00:09:32,669
the group,

209
00:09:32,669 --> 00:09:33,414
the project,

210
00:09:33,414 --> 00:09:34,160
the version,

211
00:09:34,160 --> 00:09:34,719
the path,

212
00:09:34,719 --> 00:09:35,527
and the size.

213
00:09:38,077 --> 00:09:38,864
Scroll down,

214
00:09:38,864 --> 00:09:40,307
and the hashes appear.

215
00:09:40,307 --> 00:09:43,652
The shaw one checksum is a fingerprint of the file.

216
00:09:43,652 --> 00:09:44,964
If one byte changes,

217
00:09:44,964 --> 00:09:45,685
it changes.

218
00:09:45,685 --> 00:09:48,637
Your lab asks for the one of the release jar.

219
00:09:52,187 --> 00:09:58,053
Now corp dash releases. One jar, version one dot zero dot zero. Fixed forever.

220
00:10:01,603 --> 00:10:03,106
Now the advanced part.

221
00:10:03,106 --> 00:10:06,725
Your build also downloads plugins from Maven Central,

222
00:10:06,725 --> 00:10:07,477
every time.

223
00:10:07,477 --> 00:10:10,345
Companies send that traffic through Nexus,

224
00:10:10,345 --> 00:10:11,438
so it is faster,

225
00:10:11,438 --> 00:10:12,462
and controlled.

226
00:10:13,012 --> 00:10:15,303
Open the repositories list again,

227
00:10:15,303 --> 00:10:16,900
and click maven public.

228
00:10:16,900 --> 00:10:17,872
It is a group,

229
00:10:17,872 --> 00:10:20,649
and it lists its members: maven central,

230
00:10:20,649 --> 00:10:21,690
maven releases,

231
00:10:21,690 --> 00:10:23,079
and maven snapshots.

232
00:10:23,079 --> 00:10:23,912
One address,

233
00:10:23,912 --> 00:10:25,023
for all of them.

234
00:10:28,573 --> 00:10:29,369
Tell Maven to use it.

235
00:10:29,369 --> 00:10:30,924
A mirror block in a second settings file.

236
00:10:30,924 --> 00:10:31,493
The id is corp,

237
00:10:31,493 --> 00:10:32,707
and the address is maven public.

238
00:10:32,707 --> 00:10:33,010
Show it,

239
00:10:33,010 --> 00:10:33,351
with sed.

240
00:10:35,401 --> 00:10:40,351
Build with an empty cache, through the mirror, and count the files that arrive from Nexus.

241
00:10:43,901 --> 00:10:47,975
Nexus fetches each plugin from Maven Central, and stores a copy.

242
00:11:33,525 --> 00:11:37,941
Many files, all through Nexus. The next build will find them already stored.

243
00:11:38,491 --> 00:11:39,440
In the browser,

244
00:11:39,440 --> 00:11:40,198
open browse,

245
00:11:40,198 --> 00:11:41,653
and then maven central.

246
00:11:41,653 --> 00:11:45,572
Those are the files Nexus fetched from the real Maven Central.

247
00:11:45,572 --> 00:11:46,837
They are stored now.

248
00:11:46,837 --> 00:11:47,343
A cache,

249
00:11:47,343 --> 00:11:48,923
filled by your own build.

250
00:11:54,473 --> 00:11:56,362
Next in the nexus masterclass,

251
00:11:56,362 --> 00:11:58,503
you add a dedicated deployer user,

252
00:11:58,503 --> 00:12:00,392
with only the rights it needs,

253
00:12:00,392 --> 00:12:02,217
instead of the admin account.

254
00:12:03,767 --> 00:12:04,714
Your lab task.

255
00:12:04,714 --> 00:12:08,842
Lab ninety-one installs a real Nexus on your virtual machine,

256
00:12:08,842 --> 00:12:10,601
with a project to publish.

257
00:12:10,601 --> 00:12:12,428
Lab check judges your work.

258
00:12:12,978 --> 00:12:15,165
It lives at git hub dot com,

259
00:12:15,165 --> 00:12:16,727
slash it dash waves,

260
00:12:16,727 --> 00:12:18,523
slash dev ops dash A I,

261
00:12:18,523 --> 00:12:19,382
in academy,

262
00:12:19,382 --> 00:12:19,694
lab,

263
00:12:19,694 --> 00:12:21,490
lab ninety-one dot S H.

264
00:12:22,040 --> 00:12:23,371
One: open the web page,

265
00:12:23,371 --> 00:12:25,166
log in with the first password,

266
00:12:25,166 --> 00:12:26,612
choose your own password,

267
00:12:26,612 --> 00:12:27,886
and finish the wizard.

268
00:12:28,436 --> 00:12:31,923
Two: create corp dash snapshots and corp dash releases,

269
00:12:31,923 --> 00:12:35,220
with the right version policy and deployment policy.

270
00:12:35,770 --> 00:12:38,249
Three: set the variable nexus pass,

271
00:12:38,249 --> 00:12:39,950
and deploy the snapshot,

272
00:12:39,950 --> 00:12:42,146
with dash s settings dot X M L.

273
00:12:42,146 --> 00:12:45,618
Then change the version to one dot zero dot zero,

274
00:12:45,618 --> 00:12:47,247
and deploy the release.

275
00:12:47,797 --> 00:12:49,841
Four: deploy the release again.

276
00:12:49,841 --> 00:12:50,699
It must fail.

277
00:12:50,699 --> 00:12:53,535
Save the error line into conflict dot text.

278
00:12:53,535 --> 00:12:56,964
Then find the shaw one of the release jar in browse,

279
00:12:56,964 --> 00:12:59,338
and write it into shaw one dot text.

280
00:12:59,888 --> 00:13:02,315
Five: publish one dot zero dot one,

